Notebook[{Cell["Graph Networks for Polymers in the Wolfram Language", 
   "Title"], 
  Cell[
   "A learned force field for bead-spring chains, trained by force matching", 
   "Subtitle"], Cell["\[Copyright] 2026 Computational Classnotes \[CenterDot] \
CC BY-NC-SA 4.0\nAuthors: Dara O Shayda \[CenterDot] Noor Hoshino", "Text"], 
  Cell["This notebook is the Wolfram Language edition of polymer-neural-nets. \
It does in one place what the Python notebooks 01-04 do: it simulates a \
reference polymer, turns each frame into a graph, trains a graph network to \
reproduce the forces, and then runs new simulations with the network in place \
of the true physics, including on chains twice as long as any in the training \
set.", "Text"], Cell[TextData[{"All code lives in the package PolymerNN.wl, \
kept next to this notebook. Every function there has a long comment \
explaining what it does and why. Reduced Lennard-Jones units are used \
throughout: \[CurlyEpsilon] = \[Sigma] = m = ", 
     Cell[BoxData[SubscriptBox["k", "B"]]], " = 1, and T = 1."}], "Text"], 
  Cell["1. Loading the package", "Section"], 
  Cell["SetDirectory[NotebookDirectory[]];\nGet[\"PolymerNN.wl\"];\n$PNN", 
   "Input", CellLabel -> "In[1]:="], 
  Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\[LeftAssociation]", 
      RowBox[{RowBox[{"\"kBond\"", "\[Rule]", "100.`"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"\"r0\"", "\[Rule]", "1.`"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"\"kT\"", "\[Rule]", "1.`"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"\"gamma\"", "\[Rule]", "1.`"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"\"dt\"", "\[Rule]", "0.005`"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"\"rc\"", "\[Rule]", "1.5`"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"\"mu\"", "\[Rule]", RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"0.6`", ",", 
              "0.66`", ",", "0.72`", ",", "0.78`", ",", 
              "0.8400000000000001`", ",", "0.9`", ",", "0.9600000000000001`", 
              ",", "1.02`", ",", "1.08`", ",", "1.14`", ",", "1.2`", ",", 
              "1.2599999999999998`", ",", "1.32`", ",", 
              "1.3800000000000001`", ",", "1.44`", ",", "1.5`"}], "}"}]}], 
        ",", RowBox[{"\"hidden\"", "\[Rule]", "32"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"\"rClamp\"", "\[Rule]", "0.88`"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"\"rBondMax\"", "\[Rule]", "1.45`"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"\"sigmaCore\"", "\[Rule]", "0.8`"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"\"gw\"", "\[Rule]", "277.77777777777726`"}]}], 
      "\[RightAssociation]"}]], "Output", CellLabel -> "Out[1]="], 
  Cell["$PNN holds every parameter. The bonds are harmonic springs (kBond = \
100, r0 = 1). Every pair of beads also repels through the WCA potential, a \
Lennard-Jones potential cut at its minimum 2^(1/6) and shifted to zero there. \
So the chain is a self-avoiding walk in a good solvent.", "Text"], 
  Cell["2. The reference model", "Section"], Cell["The exact forces are \
compiled (to C when a compiler is present). First check that they are minus \
the gradient of the energy, by central finite differences on one bead.", 
   "Text"], Cell["SeedRandom[1];\nx = LangevinRun[StraightChain[32], 20000, \
20000][[-1, 1]];\nh = 10.^-6;\ne[k_] := Outer[Times, UnitVector[32, 5], \
UnitVector[3, k]];\nfd = Table[-(ReferenceEnergy[x + h e[k]] - \
ReferenceEnergy[x - h e[k]])/(2 h), {k, 3}];\n{ReferenceForces[x][[5]], fd}", 
   "Input", CellLabel -> "In[2]:="], 
  Cell[BoxData[RowBox[
     {"{", RowBox[{RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{RowBox[{"-", "4.219755147435364`"}], 
            ",", RowBox[{"-", "2.9917357702483303`"}], ",", 
            "10.943906816741865`"}], "}"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{RowBox[{"-", "4.219755151524396`"}], ",", 
            RowBox[{"-", "2.9917357693420854`"}], ",", 
            "10.94390681544155`"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]], "Output", 
   CellLabel -> "Out[2]="], Cell["Langevin dynamics uses the BAOAB splitting: \
half kick, half drift, an exact Ornstein-Uhlenbeck step for the velocities, \
half drift, half kick. Generate training data: 8 independent chains of 32 \
beads, each started straight, equilibrated for 20 000 steps and then sampled \
every 100 steps (500 frames each). Two more chains of 32 and two of 64 beads \
are kept aside as test sets.", "Text"], Cell["SeedRandom[2026]; frames = \
GenerateData[32, 8, 20000, 500, 100];\nSeedRandom[2027]; test32 = \
GenerateData[32, 2, 20000, 200, 100];\nSeedRandom[2028]; test64 = \
GenerateData[64, 2, 40000, 200, 100];\n{Length[frames], \"RMS force\" -> \
Sqrt[Mean[Flatten[frames[[All, 2]]^2]]]}", "Input", CellLabel -> "In[3]:="], 
  Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"4000", ",", 
        RowBox[{"\"RMS force\"", "\[Rule]", "13.232896270926918`"}]}], 
      "}"}]], "Output", CellLabel -> "Out[3]="], 
  Cell["Graphics3D[{Gray, Tube[frames[[-1, 1]], 0.08], RGBColor[0.2, 0.4, \
0.8], Sphere[frames[[-1, 1]], 0.3]}, Boxed -> False, PlotLabel -> \"A \
reference chain, N = 32\"]", "Input", CellLabel -> "In[4]:="], 
