  Cell["3. The chain as a graph", "Section"], Cell["Beads are nodes. There \
are two kinds of edges: the N - 1 bonds, and every non-bonded pair (|i - j| > \
1). A non-bonded edge counts only when its beads are closer than rc = 1.5; a \
smooth cosine cutoff c(r) switches it off continuously at rc.", "Text"], 
  Cell["topo = ChainTopology[32];\nx = frames[[-1, 1]];\nnear = \
Select[topo[\"Pairs\"], Norm[x[[#[[1]]]] - x[[#[[2]]]]] < $PNN[\"rc\"] \
&];\nGraph3D[Range[32], Join[UndirectedEdge @@@ topo[\"Bonds\"], \
UndirectedEdge @@@ near],\n VertexCoordinates -> x, EdgeStyle -> \
Join[Thread[(UndirectedEdge @@@ topo[\"Bonds\"]) -> Directive[Thick, Black]], \
Thread[(UndirectedEdge @@@ near) -> Directive[Orange, Dashed]]],\n PlotLabel \
-> \"Bonds (black) and non-bonded edges inside rc (orange)\"]", "Input", 
   CellLabel -> "In[5]:="], 
