  Cell["Reading it from left to right. Each branch starts from the radial \
basis of its edges: bf (31\[Times]16) for the 31 bonds, nf (465\[Times]16) \
for the 465 non-bonded pairs. phiB and phiN are NetMapOperators around the \
same small chain \
(16\[RightArrow]32\[RightArrow]tanh\[RightArrow]32\[RightArrow]tanh\
\[RightArrow]1); the same weights are applied to every edge, giving one \
scalar pair force per edge (31 and 465 numbers). On the non-bonded branch, \
cut multiplies it by the cutoff c(r) from nc. repB and repN copy each scalar \
three times, and mB and mN multiply by the unit vectors bu and nu, giving the \
message m = f u on every edge (P\[Times]3). sumB and sumN are DotLayers with \
the incidence matrices Ab (32\[Times]31) and An (32\[Times]465), which add \
each message to its two beads with opposite signs. total adds the two \
branches into F, the 32\[Times]3 forces.", "Text"], 
  Cell["Parameter count: each edge network has 16\[CenterDot]32 + 32 + \
32\[CenterDot]32 + 32 + 32 + 1 = 1633 weights, so the whole model has 3266. \
The shapes for N beads are (N \[Minus] 1) bonds and (N \[Minus] 1)(N \[Minus] \
2)/2 pairs; try ForceNetGraphPlot[BuildForceNet[ChainTopology[64]]].", 
   "Text"], 
  Cell["To save the figure at print resolution next to this notebook:", 
   "Text"], Cell["Export[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[], \
\"force-net-graph.png\"}], ForceNetGraphPlot[net0], ImageResolution -> 300]", 
   "Input", CellLabel -> "In[9]:="], Cell[BoxData["\"force-net-graph.png\""], 
   "Output", CellLabel -> "Out[9]="], Cell["5. Training by force matching", 
   "Section"], Cell["The loss is the mean squared error between predicted and \
reference forces over all beads and frames. NetTrain does the \
differentiation. The two incidence matrices are frozen (learning-rate \
multiplier 0), so only the two \[CurlyPhi] networks learn. Adam is used, with \
learning rate 0.003, cut by a factor of 10 for the last 30% of training. \
Allow about 3 to 4 minutes on a laptop CPU.", "Text"], 
  Cell["SeedRandom[11];\nres = TrainForceNet[frames, test32, BatchSize -> 32, \
MaxTrainingRounds -> 300, TimeGoal -> 240,\n   LearningRate -> 0.003, Method \
-> {\"ADAM\", \"LearningRateSchedule\" -> (If[#1 < 0.7 #2, 1., 0.1] &)},\n   \
TrainingProgressReporting -> \"Panel\"];\nnet = \
res[\"TrainedNet\"];\nListLogPlot[{res[\"RoundLossList\"], \
res[\"ValidationLossList\"]}, Joined -> True, PlotLegends -> {\"training\", \
\"validation\"}, AxesLabel -> {\"round\", \"MSE\"}]", "Input", 
   CellLabel -> "In[10]:="], 
