  Cell["6. What the network learned", "Section"], 
  Cell["Because each \[CurlyPhi] is a function of one variable, it can be \
drawn and compared with the exact pair forces. Positive values push the pair \
apart.", "Text"], Cell["pf = PairForceFunctions[net];\ntrueN[r_] := \
UnitStep[2^(1/6) - r] 24 (2 r^-13 - r^-7);\ntrueB[r_] := -$PNN[\"kBond\"] (r \
- $PNN[\"r0\"]) + trueN[r];\nrr = Subdivide[0.85, 1.5, 300];\nGraphicsRow[{\n \
 ListLinePlot[{Transpose[{rr, pf[\"Bond\"][rr]}], Transpose[{rr, trueB /@ \
rr}]}, PlotStyle -> {Thick, Dashed}, PlotLegends -> {\"learned\", \"exact\"}, \
PlotLabel -> \"Bond pair force\", AxesLabel -> {\"r\", \"f\"}],\n  \
ListLinePlot[{Transpose[{rr, pf[\"NonBond\"][rr]}], Transpose[{rr, trueN /@ \
rr}]}, PlotStyle -> {Thick, Dashed}, PlotLegends -> {\"learned\", \"exact\"}, \
PlotLabel -> \"Non-bonded pair force\", AxesLabel -> {\"r\", \"f\"}]}, \
ImageSize -> 800]", "Input", CellLabel -> "In[11]:="], 
