   "Output", CellLabel -> "Out[11]="], Cell["Force errors on held-out frames. \
LearnedForces works for any chain length, because the same \[CurlyPhi] is \
applied to every edge. The 64-bead test is a length the network never saw.", 
   "Text"], Cell["lf = LearnedForces[net];\np32 = lf /@ test32[[All, 1]]; p64 \
= lf /@ test64[[All, 1]];\n<|\"RMSE N=32\" -> ForceRMSE[p32, test32[[All, \
2]]], \"RMSE N=64\" -> ForceRMSE[p64, test64[[All, 2]]],\n  \"RMS force\" -> \
Sqrt[Mean[Flatten[test64[[All, 2]]^2]]], \"max |total force|\" -> \
Max[Abs[Total[p64, {2}]]]|>", "Input", CellLabel -> "In[12]:="], 
  Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\[LeftAssociation]", 
      RowBox[{RowBox[{"\"RMSE N=32\"", "\[Rule]", "0.10795573568592085`"}], 
        ",", RowBox[{"\"RMSE N=64\"", "\[Rule]", "0.1237502198111825`"}], 
        ",", RowBox[{"\"RMS force\"", "\[Rule]", "13.5334337691266`"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"\"max |total force|\"", "\[Rule]", 
          "2.930988785010413`*^-14"}]}], "\[RightAssociation]"}]], "Output", 
   CellLabel -> "Out[12]="], 
  Cell["7. Molecular dynamics with the learned forces", "Section"], 
  Cell[TextData[{"For speed, the two learned pair forces are sampled on 4001 \
points between 0.6 and 1.6, and a compiled integrator interpolates them, as \
LAMMPS does with tabulated potentials. The table reproduces the network to \
about ", Cell[BoxData[SuperscriptBox["10", "-5"]]], 
     ". Potentials come from integrating the tabulated force."}], "Text"], 
  Cell["tab = TabulateForceField[net]; tf = TabulatedForces[tab]; te = \
TabulatedEnergy[tab];\nForceRMSE[tf /@ test64[[All, 1]], p64]", "Input", 
   CellLabel -> "In[13]:="], Cell[BoxData["0.000021564065226771452`"], 
   "Output", CellLabel -> "Out[13]="], Cell["NVE test: start one frame with \
Maxwell velocities and integrate with velocity Verlet (dt = 0.002) for 5000 \
steps. Do it once with exact forces and once with learned forces. The \
constant in the learned energy differs from the exact one, because a force \
fixes a potential only up to a constant, so the fluctuations are what to \
compare.", "Text"], Cell["SeedRandom[5]; x0 = test32[[50, 1]];\nv0 = \
RandomVariate[NormalDistribution[], {32, 3}]; v0 -= ConstantArray[Mean[v0], \
32];\nnveRef = VelocityVerletNVE[x0, v0, 5000, 0.002, ReferenceForces, \
ReferenceEnergy];\nnveNN = VelocityVerletNVE[x0, v0, 5000, 0.002, tf, \
te];\nListLinePlot[{{#1, #2 - nveRef[[1, 2]]} & @@@ nveRef, {#1, #2 - \
nveNN[[1, 2]]} & @@@ nveNN},\n PlotLegends -> {\"exact forces\", \"learned \
forces\"}, AxesLabel -> {\"t\", \"E(t) - E(0)\"}, PlotRange -> All]", 
   "Input", CellLabel -> "In[14]:="], 
